# THE PACKS ARE BYTES, NOT TEXT.
#
# Every pack carries a sha256 over its own body and a detached signature over its manifest. Git
# normalising line endings on checkout would change those bytes and every signature in the set
# would fail at once — on a fresh clone, on a colleague's Windows machine, on CI, and nowhere
# that anybody was looking when the file was committed.
#
# Written by campaign-p2/bin/p2-pack-shas.mjs in the pipeline repository. Do not edit by hand.
* -text
